    "text_frames": [
      {
        "id": "notes",
        "position": [
          2,
          1
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**SP10 \u2014 Where does the tail go?**  \n**Predict \u2192 Run \u2192 Compare \u2192 Change one tap. Run 2 s at 8 Hz.** All Delay states start at zero.  \nWord x=[1, 2, \u22121, 1] V; h=[1, 0.5, \u22120.25]. First 8 ticks warm up the periodic paths. Read n=8\u202615 at Scope times **1.125\u20262 s**.  \nLinear: [1, 2.5, \u22120.25, 0, 0.75, \u22120.25, 0, 0]. Circular 4 wraps the tail: [1.75, 2.25, \u22120.25, 0], twice. Padded 8 matches linear in this block.  \nSelect last_tap, F4: value \u22120.25 \u2192 0.5. Predict all three outputs before rerunning. The input word builders are on the left; the same three-tap FIR is on each right-hand row.  \n[Open SP10 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP10-circular-convolution/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT circular convolution](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-6-008-digital-signal-processing-spring-2011/resources/lecture-10-circular-convolution/) \u00b7 [S7 convolution implementation](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/CONVOLUTION.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 2350,
          "height": 520,
          "font_size": 24
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
